From d0ad9d3735a1d9ecbc2a8a74a7f1df98b044e8ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:43:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: render lines through an encoder interface

The logger thread rendered text and JSON with two Logger methods. They
become LogEncoder implementations (src/logging/encoder.*), so that
further formats are added as encoders without touching the capture path
or the logger's I/O: an encoder turns one LogLine (time, level,
category, thread, source location, message and flags, all captured by
the caller's ring record) and a snapshot of the logging options into a
reused buffer, on the logger thread only.

The shared building blocks (RFC 3339 times, JSON escaping, level and
category names, the text prefix, bare function names) move along. No
output changes.

(cherry picked from commit b135096c87b8cfb640c5b72abe87a5ef448608ea)

